# ── Supabase ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 1. Create a free project at https://supabase.com
# 2. Go to Settings → API and copy the values below
# 3. Run supabase/schema.sql in Database → SQL Editor
# 4. Create a public storage bucket named "openfield-images" in Storage
# 5. Rename this file to .env.local (never commit .env.local)

NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project.supabase.co
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-anon-key-here

# ── Sentry (error tracking, optional) ───────────────────────────────────────────
# 1. Create a free project at https://sentry.io (platform: Next.js)
# 2. Copy the DSN from Settings → Client Keys (DSN)
# 3. (Optional, for readable stack traces) create an internal integration /
#    auth token under Settings → Auth Tokens, and set org/project below.
# If NEXT_PUBLIC_SENTRY_DSN is left empty, Sentry is fully disabled — no errors
# are sent anywhere.

NEXT_PUBLIC_SENTRY_DSN=
SENTRY_ORG=
SENTRY_PROJECT=
SENTRY_AUTH_TOKEN=
